---
import LearnFlow from '../components/LearnFlow';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Learn BPMN · Goodsole process lab"
	description="Explore the BPMN activities, events, gateways, data, and participants used in the Goodsole process diagrams."
>
	<main class="learn-page">
		<header class="learn-page__intro">
			<p class="bpmn-page__kicker">A FIELD GUIDE TO PROCESS DIAGRAMS</p>
			<h1>Learn the language of BPMN.</h1>
			<p>
				Meet the building blocks behind the Goodsole shoe-order process. Each
				canvas uses the same interactive components as the example diagram:
				drag a node, zoom, and fit the view.
			</p>
		</header>

		<nav class="learn-toc" aria-label="BPMN node categories">
			<a href="#activities">Activities</a>
			<a href="#events">Events</a>
			<a href="#gateways">Gateways</a>
			<a href="#artifacts">Data &amp; annotations</a>
			<a href="#participants">Pools &amp; lanes</a>
		</nav>

		<LearnFlow client:only="react" />

		<aside class="learn-note">
			<strong>A note on scope</strong>
			<p>
				This gallery introduces the BPMN visual primitives implemented in this
				project. BPMN 2.0 includes additional event definitions, task variants,
				and diagram constructs; this gallery is not a complete specification
				guide or an executable process engine.
			</p>
		</aside>
	</main>
</Layout>
